WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.149
In 1925,

2
00:00:01.149 --> 00:00:03.455
Gandhi published a list of

3
00:00:03.455 --> 00:00:05.319
seven social sins.

4
00:00:05.319 --> 00:00:06.517
Each one is a thing

5
00:00:06.517 --> 00:00:08.372
without its conscience.

6
00:00:08.721 --> 00:00:10.288
Wealth without work.

7
00:00:10.288 --> 00:00:12.131
Pleasure without conscience.

8
00:00:12.131 --> 00:00:14.051
Knowledge without character.

9
00:00:14.051 --> 00:00:16.150
Commerce without morality.

10
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:18.059
Science without humanity.

11
00:00:18.059 --> 00:00:20.198
Religion without sacrifice.

12
00:00:20.198 --> 00:00:22.772
And politics without principle.

13
00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:25.237
They make strong openers in

14
00:00:25.237 --> 00:00:26.721
GS4 and essays.

15
00:00:26.721 --> 00:00:28.206
Pair one with a modern

16
00:00:28.206 --> 00:00:30.358
case. Commerce without morality,

17
00:00:30.358 --> 00:00:32.267
and a corporate fraud.

18
00:00:32.945 --> 00:00:34.946
Kant: treat people as ends,

19
00:00:34.946 --> 00:00:36.599
never only as means.

20
00:00:36.599 --> 00:00:38.752
Aristotle: virtue is the mean

21
00:00:38.752 --> 00:00:40.444
between extremes.

22
00:00:40.792 --> 00:00:42.018
Your turn.

23
00:00:42.018 --> 00:00:43.405
Which one is on the

24
00:00:43.405 --> 00:00:44.317
list?
